    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="1378" n="1366" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/8–3045:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Berlin</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-31T20:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>385. Reurtel 394 August 30.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d689-f1"/> As stated in Dept’s
                    274 August 13, negotiations for interim agency for Rhine and Danube and the
                    re-establishment of permanent agencies for international waterways will be
                    considered by the Council of Foreign Ministers in London. In order not to
                    prejudice these discussions, no agreement for a provisional organization should
                    be reached by the LTS, British and French transport divisions of the Control
                    Council and the problem should not be referred under any circumstances to the
                    quadripartite transport <pb facs="1379" n="1367" xml:id="pg1367"/> directorate
                    or other riparian states. Current problems relating to resumption of traffic
                    movement and navigation may however be worked out informally by the Control
                    Council in cooperation with the Provisional Organization for European Inland
                        Transport.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d689-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
